# Zod Schema Validation

All external input entering the API must be validated with Zod before reaching the service layer.

## Where validation lives

| Input source | Validated in | Schema lives in |
|---|---|---|
| Request body | Controller | `src/schemas/*.schema.ts` |
| Query params | Controller | `src/schemas/*.schema.ts` |
| Route params | Controller | `src/schemas/*.schema.ts` |
| Env vars | App startup | `src/config.ts` |

## Schema file conventions

```typescript
// src/schemas/traffic.schema.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

export const TrafficRecordSchema = z.object({
  sourceIp: z.string().min(1).regex(/^(\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}$/, 'must be a valid IPv4'),
  destinationApp: z.string().min(1).trim(),
  authType: z.enum(['none', 'basic', 'oauth', 'saml']),
  userId: z.string().min(1).trim(),
  timestamp: z.string().datetime(),
});

// Always export the inferred type — never write it by hand
export type TrafficRecordInput = z.infer<typeof TrafficRecordSchema>;
```

## Controller usage — always use `safeParse`

```typescript
// Request body
const result = TrafficRecordSchema.safeParse(req.body);
if (!result.success) {
  res.status(400).json({ error: 'Validation failed', details: result.error.flatten().fieldErrors });
  return;
}
const input: TrafficRecordInput = result.data; // fully typed, safe to pass to service

// Query params (strings → numbers via .transform + .pipe)
export const PaginationSchema = z.object({
  page: z.string().optional().default('1').transform(Number).pipe(z.number().int().min(1)),
  limit: z.string().optional().default('20').transform(Number).pipe(z.number().int().min(1).max(100)),
});
```

## Rules

- All schemas live in `src/schemas/` — never inline `z.object(...)` inside a controller or service
- Always use `safeParse`, never `parse` — `parse` throws and bypasses structured error responses
- Always export `z.infer<typeof Schema>` as the input type — never duplicate the type manually
- Services receive the already-validated type, never `req.body` directly
- Shared shapes (pagination, IDs) get their own reusable schema file

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ manual type checking instead of Zod
if (!req.body.userId || typeof req.body.userId !== 'string') { ... }

// ❌ parse() instead of safeParse() — throws an uncontrolled error
const input = TrafficRecordSchema.parse(req.body);

// ❌ passing raw req.body to the service
this.service.ingest(req.body);

// ❌ type duplicated by hand
type TrafficRecordInput = { sourceIp: string; destinationApp: string; ... }; // use z.infer instead

// ❌ schema defined inline in the controller
const result = z.object({ id: z.string() }).safeParse(req.params);
```
